OCaml bindings to the Oniguruma regular expression library, used by ochre's
TextMate tokenizer.

This code is a fork of ocaml-oniguruma by Alan Hu:
https://github.com/alan-j-hu/ocaml-oniguruma

It is maintained inside ochre as internal source code, with local changes:

- RegSet bindings (`Oniguruma.RegSet`)
- All missing `Options` flags (ASCII behavior, text segment,
  `not_begin_string`, `not_end_string`, etc.)
- All encodings that the C library initializes (ISO-8859-*, UTF-16/32, EUC-*,
  Shift_JIS, KOI8-R, CP1251, Big5, GB18030)
- `MatchParam` module and `search_with_param`, `match_with_param`, `scan`
- Global limit get/set functions (match stack, retry, parse depth, capture
  num, subexp call)
- Introspection: `number_of_names`, `foreach_name`, `name_to_backref_number`,
  `get_options`, `noname_group_capture_is_active`

